{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Like grapes</b> — in the manner of one finding [them] in a desert land." "And the sense of כַּעֲנָבִים בַּמִּדְבָּר (like grapes in the desert) — that there is no settlement there, [so] everyone who finds them rejoices in them." "And likewise כִּבִּכְוּרָה בְּתְאֵנָה (like the first-ripe fig on a fig tree) — and their joy was only brief, for it did not endure, for they bowed to Baal Peor and consecrated themselves for shame." "<b>For shame</b> — as in וְהַבֹּשֶׁת אָכְלָה יְגִיעַ (and shame will consume the labor), there [meaning] an idol." "<b>And they became detestable things</b> — for they defiled themselves on account of the love of the women of Midian."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:45.099779502Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}